{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794314814146,"sessionID":"ses_e3a99293bffepwQ9jkh5Z7xel0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_edr0TPJp9WvpAmwN5OVy7wzX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Form & Field\n2: \n3: A small, considered shop built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, Vite and Tailwind CSS. The catalogue is public; accounts have personal, persistent carts. Prices and totals are calculated by the server in integer cents.\n4: \n5: ## Run contract\n6: \n7: - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n8: - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n9: - The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n10: - Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n11: \n12: ## Layout\n13: \n14: - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n15: - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n16: \n17: Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n18: \n19: ## Run with Docker\n20: \n21: ```sh\n22: docker build -t form-field .\n23: docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 --env ADMIN_PASSWORD -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" form-field\n24: ```\n25: \n26: Set `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in your environment before running the container to enable the `admin` account. There is no default admin password. Without a non-empty value, admin login and admin tokens are disabled. Changing the password on restart invalidates previous admin sessions.\n27: \n28: Open the app on port 8000. The first start seeds 12 products with at least 10 units in stock. SQLite stores accounts, hashed passwords, hashed bearer tokens, products and carts in `data/shop.sqlite3`. Mount the entire data directory, including SQLite journal files, for persistence. Regular sessions last 30 days and survive restarts; sign-out revokes the token.\n29: \n30: ## Local development\n31: \n32: ```sh\n33: python3 -m venv .venv\n34: .venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock -r backend/requirements-dev.txt\n35: npm --prefix frontend ci\n36: npm --prefix frontend run build\n37: .venv/bin/python backend/app.py\n38: ```\n39: \n40: For hot reload, run `npm --prefix frontend run dev` in a second terminal. Vite proxies `/api` to the Flask server on port 8000.\n41: \n42: ## Checks\n43: \n44: ```sh\n45: .venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend -v\n46: .venv/bin/ruff check backend\n47: npm --prefix frontend run lint\n48: npm --prefix frontend run typecheck\n49: npm --prefix frontend run build\n50: ```\n51: \n52: Browser tests exercise the production frontend served by Flask, using a separate temporary SQLite database and a test-only admin password:\n53: \n54: ```sh\n55: npm --prefix frontend exec -- playwright install chromium\n56: npm --prefix frontend run test:e2e\n57: ```\n58: \n59: For an existing Chromium installation, set `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` to its executable. Browser tests require the root `.venv` from the development steps above and a current frontend build.\n60: \n61: ## API behavior\n62: \n63: - Registration returns 201. Login returns a bearer token; send it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Account usernames are case-insensitive and `admin` is reserved.\n64: - The catalogue supports `q`, `page` (default 1), and `page_size` (default 8, maximum 100). Search matches names and descriptions; results are ordered by name. Only active products are public.\n65: - Cart additions merge quantities. Quantities must be positive integers and must not exceed current stock. Adding items never changes or reserves stock. Inactive products remain stored in carts but are excluded from returned items and totals.\n66: - Another account’s cart item returns 404. Protected endpoints require a valid token (401); admin endpoints reject other accounts (403).\n67: - Product prices are non-negative and have at most two decimal places. Stock is a non-negative integer. Rejected requests return JSON with a `message` shown by the frontend.\n68: - Additional endpoints: `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/logout`, and paged `GET /api/admin/products` (including inactive products).\n69: - This app is a catalogue and cart, not a checkout or payment system.\n\n(End of file - total 69 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Form & Field\n\nA small, considered shop built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, Vite and Tailwind CSS. The catalogue is public; accounts have personal, persistent carts. Prices and totals are calculated by the server in integer cents.\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n## Run with Docker\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"# Form & Field\n\nA small, considered shop built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, Vite and Tailwind CSS. The catalogue is public; accounts have personal, persistent carts. Prices and totals are calculated by the server in integer cents.\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n## Run with Docker\n\n```sh\ndocker build -t form-field .\ndocker run --rm -p 8000:8000 --env ADMIN_PASSWORD -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" form-field\n```\n\nSet `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in your environment before running the container to enable the `admin` account. There is no default admin password. Without a non-empty value, admin login and admin tokens are disabled. Changing the password on restart invalidates previous admin sessions.\n\nOpen the app on port 8000. The first start seeds 12 products with at least 10 units in stock. SQLite stores accounts, hashed passwords, hashed bearer tokens, products and carts in `data/shop.sqlite3`. Mount the entire data directory, including SQLite journal files, for persistence. Regular sessions last 30 days and survive restarts; sign-out revokes the token.\n\n## Local development\n\n```sh\npython3 -m venv .venv\n.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock -r backend/requirements-dev.txt\nnpm --prefix frontend ci\nnpm --prefix frontend run build\n.venv/bin/python backend/app.py\n```\n\nFor hot reload, run `npm --prefix frontend run dev` in a second terminal. Vite proxies `/api` to the Flask server on port 8000.\n\n## Checks\n\n```sh\n.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend -v\n.venv/bin/ruff check backend\nnpm --prefix frontend run lint\nnpm --prefix frontend run typecheck\nnpm --prefix frontend run build\n```\n\nBrowser tests exercise the production frontend served by Flask, using a separate temporary SQLite database and a test-only admin password:\n\n```sh\nnpm --prefix frontend exec -- playwright install chromium\nnpm --prefix frontend run test:e2e\n```\n\nFor an existing Chromium installation, set `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` to its executable. Browser tests require the root `.venv` from the development steps above and a current frontend build.\n\n## API behavior\n\n- Registration returns 201. Login returns a bearer token; send it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Account usernames are case-insensitive and `admin` is reserved.\n- The catalogue supports `q`, `page` (default 1), and `page_size` (default 8, maximum 100). Search matches names and descriptions; results are ordered by name. Only active products are public.\n- Cart additions merge quantities. Quantities must be positive integers and must not exceed current stock. Adding items never changes or reserves stock. Inactive products remain stored in carts but are excluded from returned items and totals.\n- Another account’s cart item returns 404. Protected endpoints require a valid token (401); admin endpoints reject other accounts (403).\n- Product prices are non-negative and have at most two decimal places. Stock is a non-negative integer. Rejected requests return JSON with a `message` shown by the frontend.\n- Additional endpoints: `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/logout`, and paged `GET /api/admin/products` (including inactive products).\n- This app is a catalogue and cart, not a checkout or payment system.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":69,"totalLines":69,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1794314814044,"end":1794314814137}},"id":"prt_1c57f4256001IJ53uk6Lax7UTu","sessionID":"ses_e3a99293bffepwQ9jkh5Z7xel0","messageID":"msg_1c57f2cea001sC1xiRtkdsjsSR"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794314814147,"sessionID":"ses_e3a99293bffepwQ9jkh5Z7xel0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_d9Kn2Hb2UszSJPSlq1h6uRLG","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/package.json"},"output":"<path>/workspace/frontend/package.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"name\": \"app-frontend\",\n3:   \"private\": true,\n4:   \"type\": \"module\",\n5:   \"scripts\": {\n6:     \"dev\": \"vite\",\n7:     \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n8:     \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n9:     \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n10:     \"test:e2e\": \"playwright test\"\n11:   },\n12:   \"dependencies\": {\n13:     \"react\": \"19.3.1\",\n14:     \"react-dom\": \"19.3.1\"\n15:   },\n16:   \"devDependencies\": {\n17:     \"@eslint/js\": \"^9.39.2\",\n18:     \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.65.0\",\n19:     \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"^4.3.5\",\n20:     \"@types/node\": \"^24.10.1\",\n21:     \"@types/react\": \"^19.2.7\",\n22:     \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.2.3\",\n23:     \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"6.2.1\",\n24:     \"eslint\": \"^9.39.2\",\n25:     \"eslint-plugin-react-hooks\": \"^7.0.1\",\n26:     \"globals\": \"^17.0.0\",\n27:     \"tailwindcss\": \"^4.3.5\",\n28:     \"typescript\": \"^5.9.3\",\n29:     \"typescript-eslint\": \"^8.53.1\",\n30:     \"vite\": \"8.3.5\"\n31:   }\n32: }\n\n(End of file - total 32 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"name\": \"app-frontend\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n    \"test:e2e\": \"playwright test\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"react\": \"19.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.3.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@eslint/js\": \"^9.39.2\",\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.65.0\",\n    \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"^4.3.5\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"^24.10.1\",","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/frontend/package.json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"app-frontend\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n    \"test:e2e\": \"playwright test\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"react\": \"19.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.3.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@eslint/js\": \"^9.39.2\",\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.65.0\",\n    \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"^4.3.5\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"^24.10.1\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"^19.2.7\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.2.3\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"6.2.1\",\n    \"eslint\": \"^9.39.2\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-react-hooks\": \"^7.0.1\",\n    \"globals\": \"^17.0.0\",\n    \"tailwindcss\": \"^4.3.5\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.9.3\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"^8.53.1\",\n    \"vite\": \"8.3.5\"\n  }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":32,"totalLines":32,"truncated":false}},"title":"frontend/package.json","time":{"start":1794314814053,"end":1794314814143}},"id":"prt_1c57f425f001c4UPoe9Zk5pSBh","sessionID":"ses_e3a99293bffepwQ9jkh5Z7xel0","messageID":"msg_1c57f2cea001sC1xiRtkdsjsSR"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794314814154,"sessionID":"ses_e3a99293bffepwQ9jkh5Z7xel0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_UyJv96iWfzSEFoDjLmKwfcNh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/tests/shop.spec.ts"},"output":"<path>/workspace/frontend/tests/shop.spec.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import { expect, test } from \"@playwright/test\";\n2: \n3: test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {\n4:   await page.setViewportSize({ width: 1440, height: 1000 });\n5: });\n6: \n7: test(\"browsing, search, category filtering, pagination and product detail\", async ({ page }) => {\n8:   const errors: string[] = [];\n9:   page.on(\"pageerror\", (error) => errors.push(error.message));\n10:   await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n11:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: /Good things\\.\\s*For everyday living\\./ })).toBeVisible();\n12:   await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(8);\n13:   await page.screenshot({ path: \"test-results/storefront-desktop.png\", fullPage: true });\n14:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Next page\", exact: true }).click();\n15:   await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(4);\n16:   await expect(page.getByText(\"Showing 9–12 of 12\")).toBeVisible();\n17:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Home & living\", exact: true }).click();\n18:   await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(6);\n19:   await page.getByRole(\"searchbox\").fill(\"ceramic\");\n20:   await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(1);\n21:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"View Everyday ceramic mug\", exact: true }).click();\n22:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toBeVisible();\n23:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$18.00\")).toBeVisible();\n24:   await page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\");\n25:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toHaveCount(0);\n26:   await page.getByRole(\"searchbox\").fill(\"no-such-object\");\n27:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: \"Nothing here just yet.\" })).toBeVisible();\n28:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"See all objects\" }).click();\n29:   await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(8);\n30:   expect(errors).toEqual([]);\n31: });\n32: \n33: test(\"registration, sign-in, saved cart, stepper and server rejection messages\", async ({ page, request }) => {\n34:   const username = `shopper-${Date.now()}`;\n35:   await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n36:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Add Amber glass vase to cart\", exact: true }).click();\n37:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Create an account\", exact: true }).click();\n38:   await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Username\" }).fill(username);\n39:   await page.getByLabel(\"Password\", { exact: true }).fill(\"shop-test-password\");\n40:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Create account\", exact: true }).click();\n41:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toHaveCount(0);\n42:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n43:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true }).click();\n44:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$32.00\", { exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);\n45:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Increase quantity of Amber glass vase\" }).click();\n46:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$64.00\", { exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);\n47:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Decrease quantity of Amber glass vase\" }).click();\n48:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$32.00\", { exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);\n49:   const adminLogin = await request.post(\"/api/auth/login\", { data: { username: \"admin\", password: \"browser-test-admin-secret\" } });\n50:   const { token } = await adminLogin.json() as { token: string };\n51:   const headers = { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` };\n52:   const result = await request.get(\"/api/products?q=amber\");\n53:   const { items: [product] } = await result.json() as { items: { id: number; stock: number; price: number }[] };\n54:   try {\n55:     await request.patch(`/api/admin/products/${product.id}`, { headers, data: { price: 19.99, stock: 1 } });\n56:     await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Increase quantity of Amber glass vase\" }).click();\n57:     await expect(page.getByRole(\"alert\")).toContainText(\"Only 1 available\");\n58:     await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Close dialog\" }).click();\n59:     await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true }).click();\n60:     await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$19.99\", { exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);\n61:     await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Close dialog\" }).click();\n62:     await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign out\", exact: true }).click();\n63:     await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n64:     await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n65:     await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Username\" }).fill(username);\n66:     await page.getByLabel(\"Password\", { exact: true }).fill(\"shop-test-password\");\n67:     await page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n68:     await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n69:     await page.reload();\n70:     await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n71:     await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true }).click();\n72:     await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Remove Amber glass vase\", exact: true }).click();\n73:     await expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: \"Good things are waiting.\" })).toBeVisible();\n74:   } finally {\n75:     await request.patch(`/api/admin/products/${product.id}`, { headers, data: { price: product.price, stock: product.stock } });\n76:   }\n77: });\n78: \n79: test(\"admin adds a product, updates stock and price, hides and restores it\", async ({ page, request }) => {\n80:   await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n81:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n82:   await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Username\" }).fill(\"admin\");\n83:   await page.getByLabel(\"Password\", { exact: true }).fill(\"browser-test-admin-secret\");\n84:   await page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n85:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Manage products\", exact: true }).click();\n86:   const name = `A browser test object ${Date.now()}`;\n87:   await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Product name\" }).fill(name);\n88:   await page.getByRole(\"spinbutton\", { name: \"Price ($)\", exact: true }).fill(\"25.50\");\n89:   await page.getByRole(\"spinbutton\", { name: \"Stock\", exact: true }).fill(\"15\");\n90:   await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Description\" }).fill(\"A thoughtfully made object.\");\n91:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Add product\", exact: true }).click();\n92:   await expect(page.locator(\"main\").getByRole(\"status\")).toContainText(\"added at $25.50\");\n93:   const row = page.getByRole(\"row\").filter({ hasText: name });\n94:   await expect(row).toBeVisible();\n95:   await row.getByRole(\"spinbutton\", { name: `Price for ${name}`, exact: true }).fill(\"30.00\");\n96:   await row.getByRole(\"spinbutton\", { name: `Stock for ${name}`, exact: true }).fill(\"0\");\n97:   await row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true }).click();\n98:   await expect(page.locator(\"main\").getByRole(\"status\")).toContainText(\"Product saved\");\n99:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Back to the collection\" }).click();\n100:   await page.getByRole(\"searchbox\").fill(name);\n101:   await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(1);\n102:   await expect(page.getByText(\"Out of stock\", { exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n103:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: `Add ${name} to cart`, exact: true })).toBeDisabled();\n104:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Manage products\", exact: true }).click();\n105:   await row.getByRole(\"checkbox\", { name: `Active status for ${name}`, exact: true }).uncheck();\n106:   await row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true }).click();\n107:   await expect(row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true })).toBeDisabled();\n108:   const hidden = await request.get(`/api/products?q=${encodeURIComponent(name)}`);\n109:   expect((await hidden.json() as { total: number }).total).toBe(0);\n110:   await row.getByRole(\"checkbox\", { name: `Active status for ${name}`, exact: true }).check();\n111:   await row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true }).click();\n112:   await expect(row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true })).toBeDisabled();\n113:   const visible = await request.get(`/api/products?q=${encodeURIComponent(name)}`);\n114:   expect((await visible.json() as { total: number }).total).toBe(1);\n115: });\n116: \n117: test(\"mobile layout fits and account dialog can be dismissed with the keyboard\", async ({ page }) => {\n118:   await page.setViewportSize({ width: 390, height: 844 });\n119:   await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n120:   await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(8);\n121:   expect(await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth)).toBe(true);\n122:   await page.screenshot({ path: \"test-results/storefront-mobile.png\", fullPage: true });\n123:   await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n124:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toBeVisible();\n125:   const bounds = await page.getByRole(\"dialog\").boundingBox();\n126:   expect(bounds?.width).toBeLessThan(390);\n127:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Username\" })).toBeFocused();\n128:   await page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\");\n129:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toHaveCount(0);\n130:   await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true })).toBeFocused();\n131: });\n\n(End of file - total 131 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import { expect, test } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\ntest.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 1440, height: 1000 });\n});\n\ntest(\"browsing, search, category filtering, pagination and product detail\", async ({ page }) => {\n  const errors: string[] = [];\n  page.on(\"pageerror\", (error) => errors.push(error.message));\n  await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: /Good things\\.\\s*For everyday living\\./ })).toBeVisible();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(8);\n  await page.screenshot({ path: \"test-results/storefront-desktop.png\", fullPage: true });\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Next page\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(4);\n  await expect(page.getByText(\"Showing 9–12 of 12\")).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Home & living\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(6);\n  await page.getByRole(\"searchbox\").fill(\"ceramic\");\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(1);","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/frontend/tests/shop.spec.ts","text":"import { expect, test } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\ntest.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 1440, height: 1000 });\n});\n\ntest(\"browsing, search, category filtering, pagination and product detail\", async ({ page }) => {\n  const errors: string[] = [];\n  page.on(\"pageerror\", (error) => errors.push(error.message));\n  await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: /Good things\\.\\s*For everyday living\\./ })).toBeVisible();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(8);\n  await page.screenshot({ path: \"test-results/storefront-desktop.png\", fullPage: true });\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Next page\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(4);\n  await expect(page.getByText(\"Showing 9–12 of 12\")).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Home & living\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(6);\n  await page.getByRole(\"searchbox\").fill(\"ceramic\");\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(1);\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"View Everyday ceramic mug\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toBeVisible();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$18.00\")).toBeVisible();\n  await page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\");\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toHaveCount(0);\n  await page.getByRole(\"searchbox\").fill(\"no-such-object\");\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: \"Nothing here just yet.\" })).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"See all objects\" }).click();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(8);\n  expect(errors).toEqual([]);\n});\n\ntest(\"registration, sign-in, saved cart, stepper and server rejection messages\", async ({ page, request }) => {\n  const username = `shopper-${Date.now()}`;\n  await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Add Amber glass vase to cart\", exact: true }).click();\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Create an account\", exact: true }).click();\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Username\" }).fill(username);\n  await page.getByLabel(\"Password\", { exact: true }).fill(\"shop-test-password\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Create account\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toHaveCount(0);\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$32.00\", { exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Increase quantity of Amber glass vase\" }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$64.00\", { exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Decrease quantity of Amber glass vase\" }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$32.00\", { exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);\n  const adminLogin = await request.post(\"/api/auth/login\", { data: { username: \"admin\", password: \"browser-test-admin-secret\" } });\n  const { token } = await adminLogin.json() as { token: string };\n  const headers = { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` };\n  const result = await request.get(\"/api/products?q=amber\");\n  const { items: [product] } = await result.json() as { items: { id: number; stock: number; price: number }[] };\n  try {\n    await request.patch(`/api/admin/products/${product.id}`, { headers, data: { price: 19.99, stock: 1 } });\n    await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Increase quantity of Amber glass vase\" }).click();\n    await expect(page.getByRole(\"alert\")).toContainText(\"Only 1 available\");\n    await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Close dialog\" }).click();\n    await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true }).click();\n    await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByText(\"$19.99\", { exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);\n    await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Close dialog\" }).click();\n    await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign out\", exact: true }).click();\n    await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n    await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n    await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Username\" }).fill(username);\n    await page.getByLabel(\"Password\", { exact: true }).fill(\"shop-test-password\");\n    await page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n    await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n    await page.reload();\n    await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n    await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Open cart, 1 item\", exact: true }).click();\n    await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Remove Amber glass vase\", exact: true }).click();\n    await expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: \"Good things are waiting.\" })).toBeVisible();\n  } finally {\n    await request.patch(`/api/admin/products/${product.id}`, { headers, data: { price: product.price, stock: product.stock } });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"admin adds a product, updates stock and price, hides and restores it\", async ({ page, request }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Username\" }).fill(\"admin\");\n  await page.getByLabel(\"Password\", { exact: true }).fill(\"browser-test-admin-secret\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"dialog\").getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Manage products\", exact: true }).click();\n  const name = `A browser test object ${Date.now()}`;\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Product name\" }).fill(name);\n  await page.getByRole(\"spinbutton\", { name: \"Price ($)\", exact: true }).fill(\"25.50\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"spinbutton\", { name: \"Stock\", exact: true }).fill(\"15\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Description\" }).fill(\"A thoughtfully made object.\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Add product\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"main\").getByRole(\"status\")).toContainText(\"added at $25.50\");\n  const row = page.getByRole(\"row\").filter({ hasText: name });\n  await expect(row).toBeVisible();\n  await row.getByRole(\"spinbutton\", { name: `Price for ${name}`, exact: true }).fill(\"30.00\");\n  await row.getByRole(\"spinbutton\", { name: `Stock for ${name}`, exact: true }).fill(\"0\");\n  await row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.locator(\"main\").getByRole(\"status\")).toContainText(\"Product saved\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Back to the collection\" }).click();\n  await page.getByRole(\"searchbox\").fill(name);\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(1);\n  await expect(page.getByText(\"Out of stock\", { exact: true })).toBeVisible();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: `Add ${name} to cart`, exact: true })).toBeDisabled();\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Manage products\", exact: true }).click();\n  await row.getByRole(\"checkbox\", { name: `Active status for ${name}`, exact: true }).uncheck();\n  await row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true })).toBeDisabled();\n  const hidden = await request.get(`/api/products?q=${encodeURIComponent(name)}`);\n  expect((await hidden.json() as { total: number }).total).toBe(0);\n  await row.getByRole(\"checkbox\", { name: `Active status for ${name}`, exact: true }).check();\n  await row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(row.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\", exact: true })).toBeDisabled();\n  const visible = await request.get(`/api/products?q=${encodeURIComponent(name)}`);\n  expect((await visible.json() as { total: number }).total).toBe(1);\n});\n\ntest(\"mobile layout fits and account dialog can be dismissed with the keyboard\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 390, height: 844 });\n  await page.goto(\"/\", { waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\" });\n  await expect(page.locator(\"#collection article\")).toHaveCount(8);\n  expect(await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth)).toBe(true);\n  await page.screenshot({ path: \"test-results/storefront-mobile.png\", fullPage: true });\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toBeVisible();\n  const bounds = await page.getByRole(\"dialog\").boundingBox();\n  expect(bounds?.width).toBeLessThan(390);\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"textbox\", { name: \"Username\" })).toBeFocused();\n  await page.keyboard.press(\"Escape\");\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"dialog\")).toHaveCount(0);\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: true })).toBeFocused();\n});","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":131,"totalLines":131,"truncated":false}},"title":"frontend/tests/shop.spec.ts","time":{"start":1794314814035,"end":1794314814151}},"id":"prt_1c57f424c001AbYSjYwPKukyLb","sessionID":"ses_e3a99293bffepwQ9jkh5Z7xel0","messageID":"msg_1c57f2cea001sC1xiRtkdsjsSR"}}
